          "text": "Yes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-47",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**\\*1.8 By selecting \"Yes\", I confirm I am not an employee and do not have immediate family members who are employees or directors at American Public Media Group.\\*\\***"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-49",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-48",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Answer"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-50",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Yes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-51",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**\\*1.9 By selecting \"Yes\", I accept the Next Challenge's [Official Rules](https://www.thenextchallenge.com/rules)\\*\\***"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-53",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-52",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Answer"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-54",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Yes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-55",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-56",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**\\*2.1 Please provide a brief description of your startup (\\<280 characters)\\*\\***"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-58",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-57",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Answer"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-59",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[Docket.tv](http://docket.tv/) is a next-gen content management and distribution platform for public access TV and independent broadcasters, modernizing scheduling, audience engagement, and multi-platform delivery for an industry in transition."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-60",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**\\*2.2 What problem does your startup solve? (\\<1,800 characters)\\*\\***"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-62",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-61",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Answer"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-63",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Public access TV is under siege and must evolve to survive. As cable subscriptions decline, the PEG (Public, Educational, Government) channel ecosystem faces existential challenges: reduced funding, outdated technology, and difficulty connecting with modern audiences."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-64",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The 1,600+ public access stations across America face three critical problems:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-65",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **Operational inefficiencies with outdated technology**: Most stations rely on legacy broadcast automation systems that are expensive ($10K-$50K upfront), difficult to maintain, and often end-of-life. These systems frequently require on-site management and lack modern remote capabilities—a pain point highlighted during the pandemic when many stations struggled to stay on-air."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-66",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **Absence of user-friendly online tools**: Current systems force staff to enter program information multiple times across different platforms (once for broadcast, again for websites, etc.), creating redundant work for already understaffed operations. Critical features like multi-platform distribution to OTT apps, streaming services, and social media are either missing or require expensive add-ons."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-67",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **Disconnection from digital audiences**: As viewers cut the cord, public access stations struggle to remain relevant without modern web and mobile experiences. Their vital community content (local news, government transparency, cultural programming) reaches fewer people despite its importance in filling gaps left by shrinking local journalism."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-68",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[Docket.tv](http://docket.tv/) solves these problems with a cloud-based platform that streamlines content management and scheduling while enabling multi-platform distribution. Our system integrates with existing broadcast infrastructure (like Cablecast APIs) while adding modern capabilities: remote management, automated web/social scheduling, and interactive audience features."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-69",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "By modernizing public access TV's infrastructure, [Docket.tv](http://docket.tv/) helps preserve a vital community resource at exactly the moment when local independent media is most needed. We're ensuring that public access TV can continue its mission of democratic expression, local accountability, and community connection in the digital age."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-70",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**\\*2.3 Minimum viable product (MVP), working prototype, or beta\\*\\***"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-72",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-71",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Answer"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-73",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[Docket.tv](http://docket.tv/)'s MVP is currently live with our first partner organization in Minneapolis. Our platform provides:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-74",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. A cloud-based TV guide CMS with drag-and-drop scheduling functionality, allowing broadcasters to manage their content calendar remotely through any web browser"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-75",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. Direct integration with Cablecast API for synchronizing broadcast schedules across platforms"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-76",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. Automated web publishing that eliminates duplicate data entry, with embeddable widgets for station websites"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-77",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. Viewer-facing features including a searchable program guide, show/episode details, and watch notifications"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-78",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "5. Basic analytics dashboard tracking content performance and audience engagement"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-79",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Our next development phase will add interactive viewer features (polls, feedback), expanded multi-platform distribution (OTT apps, social media), and enhanced analytics. We're currently in discussions with several community media centers for pilot partnerships, including organizations in the Midwest and East Coast."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-80",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The initial response validates our approach: station managers particularly appreciate the remote management capabilities and the elimination of duplicate work across platforms. Early user feedback has already shaped our roadmap, with particular emphasis on flexible integration options to accommodate the diverse technical setups across the public access ecosystem."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-81",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**\\*2.4 How do you plan to grow your startup? (\\<1,800 characters)\\*\\***"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-83",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-82",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Answer"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-84",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Our growth strategy focuses on three parallel tracks:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-85",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**1. Direct Adoption by Key Innovators (Years 1-2)**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-86",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We'll target forward-thinking community media centers as early adopters—organizations like PhillyCAM, Grand Rapids Community Media Center, and Community Media Access Collaborative (Fresno). These flagship customers will provide both revenue and crucial case studies. We've identified 50+ stations actively seeking modern solutions, particularly those with aging systems from vendors like Leightronix and TelVue."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-87",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**2. Strategic Partnerships for Scale (Years 2-3)**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-88",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We'll leverage industry networks to accelerate distribution:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-89",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Partner with state PEG associations (like MassAccess or Wisconsin Community Media) to offer white-labeled or discounted solutions to their member stations"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-90",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Integrate with government platforms (Granicus, Swagit, CivicPlus) to reach municipal channels"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-91",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Collaborate with nonprofits like the Alliance for Community Media to develop grant-funded initiatives supporting technology upgrades"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-92",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**3. Financial Sustainability via Tiered SaaS Model**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-93",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Our pricing model balances accessibility with sustainable growth:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-94",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Basic tier ($49/month): Single-channel scheduling, web integration"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-95",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Professional tier ($199/month): Multi-channel capabilities, full customization, priority support"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-96",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Enterprise solutions: Custom pricing for white-labeled deployments or municipal networks"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-97",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This SaaS approach provides predictable annual revenue while aligning with how stations budget. We'll offer multi-year discounts to encourage longer commitments, which stations often prefer for planning purposes."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-98",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Funding Strategy**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-99",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Beyond direct revenue, we're pursuing strategic funding to accelerate adoption:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-100",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Media innovation grants from foundations like Knight, Democracy Fund"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-101",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Partnerships with public media organizations for pilot programs"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-102",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Creative models where local foundations sponsor Docket adoption for community stations"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-103",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "With 1,600+ PEG stations and 3,000+ community media outlets nationally, capturing just 10% of this market would create a sustainable business while transforming an essential civic media infrastructure."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-104",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-105",
      "type": "paragraph",
